8 148.9L189.3 148.0L190.9 147.1L192.4 146.2L193.9 145.2L195.5 144.3L197.0 143.4L198.6 142.4L200.1 141.4L201.7 140.5L203.2 139.5L204.7 138.5L206.3 137.5L207.8 136.5L209.4 135.5L210.9 134.5L212.5 133.4L214.0 132.4L215.5 131.4L217.1 130.3L218.6 129.2L220.2 128.2L221.7 127.1L223.3 126.0L224.8 124.9L226.3 123.8L227.9 122.7L229.4 121.6L231.0 120.5L232.5 119.3L234.1 118.2L235.6 117.1L237.1 115.9L238.7 114.7L240.2 113.6L241.8 112.4L243.3 111.2L244.9 110.0L246.4 108.8L247.9 107.6L249.5 106.4L251.0 105.1L252.6 103.9L254.1 102.7L255.7 101.4L257.2 100.1L258.7 98.9L260.3 97.6L261.8 96.3L263.4 95.0L264.9 93.7L266.5 92.4L268.0 91.1L269.5 89.8L271.1 88.4L272.6 87.1L274.2 85.8L275.7 84.4L277.3 83.0L278.8 81.7L280.3 80.3L281.9 78.9L283.4 77.5L285.0 76.1L286.5 74.7L288.1 73.3L289.6 71.8L291.1 70.4L292.7 69.0L294.2 67.5L295.8 66.0L297.3 64.6L298.9 63.1L300.4 61.6L301.9 60.1L303.5 58.6L305.0 57.1L306.6 55.6L308.1 54.1L309.7 52.5L311.2 51.0L312.7 49.5L314.3 47.9L315.8 46.3L317.4 44.8L318.9 43.2L320.5 41.6L322.0 40.0\" class=\"tq\"></path><text x=\"105.8\" y=\"116.6\" class=\"lb k-halo\" text-anchor=\"start\">speed</text><text x=\"244.9\" y=\"98.0\" class=\"lb k-halo\" text-anchor=\"end\">torque</text><text x=\"336\" y=\"262\" class=\"mu k-halo\" text-anchor=\"end\">sketch from the ideal rule</text></svg></div></div></div>","h":276},{"kind":"show","name":"Where it is used","text":"Used for: Crane hoists, lifts and large excavators, where big starting torque matters. Also traction, such as railway locomotives.\n\nHistory: In 1907 the US Navy used series motors on boat cranes, for their starting torque.\n\nCoupling: Couple it directly or through gears. Then the load is far less likely to come off. Never use a belt, which can break.\n\nProtection: It must have overspeed protection. Its starter has a no-load release that lets go if the current falls.","svg":null,"alt":"load series motor geared, never belted gears hoist drum","html":"<div class=\"pz\" id=\"pz\"><div id=\"prog\"></div><div id=\